    "All external facing materials, treatments and finishes shall be similar to those of the original building and maintained and retained thereafter. This applies unless differences are shown on the drawings we have approved. \r\rReason: To ensure that the extension harmonises with the existing building and to ensure compliance with Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The development hereby approved shall be constructed in accordance with the approved Flood Risk Assessment dated January 2026. Prior to first occupation of  the extension, documentary evidence that the approved flood resilience measures have been implemented must be submitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing together with confirmation that the development has been registered with the EA's Flood Warning Service. All of the approved measures must  thereafter be retained for as long as the development is in existence.  \r\rReason: To comply with Government Standing Advice and Policy 31 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018",
